   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>I am currently able to display a logo on a shinyapp using the following:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  output$image1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderImage</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    filename </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;logo.gif&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      src </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> filename</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      filetype </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;image/gif&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">},</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> deleteFile</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>In the above case, the file is a local file.<br><br>I would like to create an app that allows the user to display images from a non-public S3 bucket on AWS.<br><br>I am somewhat new to interfacing with S3, and I am currently using the aws.s3 and aws.signature libraries.<br><br>I am able to display the contents of a bucket using:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aws</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aws</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">signature</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>getB </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  a </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aws</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">s3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">getbucket</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bucket </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;bucketname&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>                         key </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;mykey&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                         secret </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;mySecret&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">a</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><br><br>and <br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">output$text1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderText</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> getB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><br>I am not sure of the next step.  Does an image have to be saved locally, before being displayed?  Can it be displayed directly by giving the file path (e.g.  <a href=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucketname/logo.gif\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucketname/logo.gif&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396571301000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1DECvtZwXQPzcmcP-eYQi9\">https://s3.amazonaws.com/bucketname/logo.gif</a>)?  I have tried this but it does not work.<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
